"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include a negative surgical margin (0.0), absence of seminal vesicle invasion (0.0), and absence of lymphovascular invasion (0.0). The preoperative PSA was elevated at 11. The surgical pathology showed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological T2 stage with no extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the absence of lymph node removal, as nodal status is documented as 'no nodes removed,' which widens uncertainty. Furthermore, the biopsy finding of Acinar adenocarcinoma was documented, and the biopsy grade was consistent with the prostatectomy specimen. The postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are unknown, which significantly limits the certainty of recurrence risk assessment. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and trajectory would be crucial to revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 57.15 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 37.15–77.15 months; its coverage has not been validated."
